description: Navigation rules: centralized ROUTES and navigation utilities, no hardcoded route strings.
globs: "client/app/**/*.tsx, client/lib/**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

## Navigation patterns

- Define all route strings in a centralized `ROUTES` constant for maintainability.
- No hardcoded route strings in components.
- Use `useRouter` from `next/navigation` for programmatic navigation.

## Example

```ts
// lib/constants/routes.ts
export const ROUTES = {
	HOME: "/",
	LOGIN: "/login",
	DASHBOARD: "/dashboard",
	USERS: "/users",
	USER_EDIT: (id: string) => `/users/${id}/edit`,
	ROLES: "/roles",
	ROLE_EDIT: (id: string) => `/roles/${id}/edit`,
} as const;

// Usage in component
import { ROUTES } from "@/lib/constants/routes";
router.push(ROUTES.USER_EDIT(userId));
```
